:db/id "q-7026" :question/id #uuid "8cbf7aea-3141-5c94-a26f-5d2ecaa8695b" :question/math-academy-id "q-7026" :question/is-example false :question/problem "For the function $f(x)$ defined by $f(x)=-4x+5,$ find ${f}^{-1}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=-4x+5\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=-4y+5\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-4y+5 \\\\ 4y & =-x+5 \\\\ y & =\\frac{-x+5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{-x+5}{4}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7026/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15cd299b-c720-5bf6-814c-2bef2c839e48"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7026"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109454/selection/2c2b13a91cce30588d9d0bf70b65644c875810d949307b9b10114cc6e2e8ae21" :answer/id #uuid "514beb07-75c5-5147-895e-b5c2ea8287db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=4x+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109454/selection/3b3b88c95e390926bad4d2ba5ef144dd71ea8465ed49c784f1cffd9697b15fdd" :answer/id #uuid "5c217281-2115-5d36-821e-9cab4043140e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=-2x+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109454/selection/6e660d6a30e484e7f2e94758af81a8a6193ce7952a6e7f414d31a4e52a6e79c5" :answer/id #uuid "ae6d4836-48c1-589e-80ce-ea141874e38b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=x-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109454/selection/2db2e14339948c6b6318298b632e0d7d1f01c8ca4d5241b6afc04648e0c123df" :answer/id #uuid "cae5cdab-9cd4-5caa-89d6-e129e85e3f2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=-4x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109454/selection/8542ddad84f0c069bb9fe041bbe93c55be4f41ec7a570e15791515b2426b1aa7" :answer/id #uuid "57186b05-2ab8-552b-a265-1963c714c682" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109454/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e9d85c7-6bfb-59ec-b26b-503715132795" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109454/selection/2c2b13a91cce30588d9d0bf70b65644c875810d949307b9b10114cc6e2e8ae21" :answer-field/choices ["q-109454/selection/2c2b13a91cce30588d9d0bf70b65644c875810d949307b9b10114cc6e2e8ae21" "q-109454/selection/3b3b88c95e390926bad4d2ba5ef144dd71ea8465ed49c784f1cffd9697b15fdd" "q-109454/selection/6e660d6a30e484e7f2e94758af81a8a6193ce7952a6e7f414d31a4e52a6e79c5" "q-109454/selection/2db2e14339948c6b6318298b632e0d7d1f01c8ca4d5241b6afc04648e0c123df" "q-109454/selection/8542ddad84f0c069bb9fe041bbe93c55be4f41ec7a570e15791515b2426b1aa7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109454" :question/id #uuid "c52666cc-5406-50c8-942e-f5363c466d39" :question/math-academy-id "q-109454" :question/is-example false :question/problem "What is the inverse of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{4}x-1?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{4}x-1\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{4}y-1\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{4}y-1 \\\\ x+1 & =\\frac{1}{4}y \\\\ 4(x+1) & =y \\\\ 4x+4 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=4x+4\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-109454/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15cd299b-c720-5bf6-814c-2bef2c839e48"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109454"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-218691/field-1/33c2b0246be43e3f403d2ee4575b7cc2736ecbf8f22d4787099264d679a263f7" :answer/id #uuid "747f95c7-7cab-512c-8073-ce45ec924